        "slideId": "s16",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Third: Respect the Fairness Impossibility Theorem—Demographic Parity, Equalized Odds, and Predictive Parity cannot coexist when base rates differ, so document deliberate normative choices. Fourth: Favor distributive justice over aggregate utility—evaluate systems by their least-advantaged cohort. Fifth: Provide axiomatic transparency and recourse via Shapley attribution. Next in Lesson 3.3, we investigate Utility Dilemmas and Real-World Consequences!",
