        "slide": 2,
        "slideId": "s2",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Slide 2 presents our architectural decision framework for field collection engineering. When raw streaming telemetry arrives from field sensors, mobile devices, or third-party feeds, it must pass through systematic validation gates before reaching cold storage or model training tables. First, we examine spatial and temporal metadata: are coordinate reference systems aligned between WGS84 and local UTM projections, and are clocks synchronized via cross-correlation? If not, naive joins produce catastrophic spatial and temporal drift. Second, we evaluate participant selection: is participation voluntary or subject to survivorship? If selection correlates with unobserved outcomes, we apply Heckman's two-step model with an exclusion restriction variable. Third, for multi-sensor streams with varying noise, we deploy Kalman filter fusion to achieve minimum-variance state estimates. Finally, automated pre-ingestion assertion gates enforce schema, range, and uniqueness bounds.",
