            "text": "Because high RPM and low fuel flow cannot happen together physically in a running engine! Mathematically, inverting a 2-by-2 correlation matrix with r equals 0.96 divides off-diagonal discrepancies by 1 minus r squared, which is only 0.0784—multiplying squared deviations perpendicular to the correlation cigar by nearly 13x!",
