            "text": "Look closely at the False Positive Rate denominator, Kaito. Suppose you have 100 real cancer cases and 100,000 healthy scans. If your detector raises 1,000 false alarms just to catch 90 cancers, your False Positive Rate is 1,000 divided by 100,000, which equals only 1%!",
            "dock": "main",
