        "slideIndex": 7,
        "turn": 14,
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "The ordered eigenvalues lambda 1 greater than or equal to lambda 2 measure exact projected variance along each principal axis. Summing the top k eigenvalues over total trace variance defines the Cumulative Explained Variance Ratio EVR sub k. Plotting the Scree spectrum exposes intrinsic low-rank structure, while a 2D Biplot overlays scaled loading arrows to reveal which raw sensors drive each principal axis—always remember to z-standardize features beforehand when physical measurement scales differ!",
        "start": 296.904,
        "end": 327.312,
