        "slideIndex": 9,
        "turn": 21,
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "On heavy-tailed streams like network latency or lognormal bursts, Chauvenet commits two fatal errors: first, over-rejecting valid Pareto tails; second, outlier masking—because sample standard deviation s has zero breakdown point, one extreme spike inflates denominator root 2 s so secondary outliers vanish!",
