        "text": "Congratulations on completing Lesson 3.11 and the entire Track 3 curriculum! We have traversed from classical Sweeney quasi-identifier linkage and the Obermeyer clinical cost proxy, through differential privacy Laplace mechanisms, GDPR statutory fines, cyber breach dwell times, zero-trust incident response, and algorithmic impact assessments, to the frontier of generative AI security. Remember our five core takeaways: first, deduplicate pretraining corpora before training; second, bound membership inference attacks via DP-SGD; third, certify synthetic data deniability with DP-CTGAN; fourth, neutralize federated gradient inversion with Bonawitz Secure Aggregation; and fifth, enforce data sovereignty by design through client-side European key custody. You are now equipped with the mathematical and legal tools to architect ethical, robust, and privacy-preserving data systems in the foundation model era. Thank you for your exceptional dedication throughout Track 3!",
