        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "It proves that among all possible matrices M of rank k, the truncated singular value expansion X-hat-k uniquely minimizes the Frobenius reconstruction error. The discarded error equals the exact sum of the remaining singular values squared, or n minus one times the sum of discarded eigenvalues.",
