        "slideId": "s10",
        "slideIndex": 9,
        "turn": 18,
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "The gradient decomposes into attractive forces pulling genuine high-dimensional neighbors together where p-ij exceeds q-ij, and repulsive forces pushing all points apart. Crucially, because p-ij is zero between points in separate clusters, the attractive force between clusters is strictly zero. Inter-cluster distances in t-SNE are arbitrary artifacts of the random seed!",
