        "slideId": "s11",
        "slideIndex": 10,
        "turn": 20,
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "UMAP models high-dimensional data as a fuzzy simplicial complex on a Riemannian manifold. Unlike t-SNE's KL divergence, UMAP optimizes fuzzy set cross-entropy. Crucially, the second term creates continuous global repulsion across all non-neighboring pairs, preserving global manifold geometry and macro distances.",
