        "slideId": "s8",
        "slideIndex": 7,
        "turn": 14,
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "When testing m independent null hypotheses at alpha equals 0.05, the Family-Wise Error Rate explodes as 1 minus 0.95 to the power of m. At 100 tests, the probability of at least one false positive exceeds 99.4 percent. Uncorrected EDA is mathematically guaranteed to find spurious correlations.",
