        "slideIndex": 8,
        "turn": 16,
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "At 10,000 tests, Bonferroni demands a p-value below 5 times 10 to the minus 6. Statistical power collapses toward zero, throwing away genuine discoveries. In 1995, Yoav Benjamini and Yosef Hochberg solved this dilemma by shifting the objective from FWER to the False Discovery Rate.",
