        "text": "Definition 12.1.3 examines the tension between Amdahl's Law and Gustafson's Law. Amdahl governs strong scaling, where problem size is fixed: if serial fraction 1 minus p is five percent, theoretical speedup can never exceed twenty, no matter how many thousands of nodes you add.",
