        "slide": 2,
        "slideId": "s2",
        "slideIndex": 1,
        "turnIndex": 1,
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Critically, a Labeling Function is allowed to abstain by returning zero. Unlike a classical classifier that forces a guess on every sample, an LF fires only when its pattern is triggered—allowing unsupervised factor graphs to infer rule accuracy and train deep end models that generalize beyond the rules themselves.",
