        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Rule 1: Anchor all window aggregations on Event-Time Watermarks. Rule 2: Bound sliding window state multipliers to prevent memory explosion. Rule 3: Enforce credit-based backpressure under Little's Law. Rule 4: Partition distributed commit logs to prevent broker bottlenecks. Master these, and your real-time data pipelines will never falter.",
