        "slideId": "s1",
        "slideIndex": 0,
        "turnIndex": 0,
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Welcome to Lesson 11.8: Practical Applications of Self-Supervised Learning: Pretraining, Linear Probing, and Downstream Tasks. Pretraining a foundation encoder on millions of unannotated images or sensor streams builds a structured representation space; downstream adaptation transfers this general-purpose manifold to operational industrial tasks where manual gold annotations are scarce, expensive, or hazardous to acquire.",
