        "turnIndex": 0,
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Machine learning teams deploy self-supervised encoders across four canonical operational paradigms: linear probing, non-parametric k-NN retrieval, parameter-efficient fine-tuning via LoRA, and end-to-end few-shot fine-tuning. Each protocol represents a distinct compromise between computational cost, labeled data requirements, and catastrophic forgetting risk.",
