        "text": "When transferring a self-supervised encoder to a new target domain, how do we bound downstream generalization error? Ben-David and colleagues proved that target risk is upper-bounded by source risk plus half the H-delta-H divergence between feature distributions, plus the irreducible joint error lambda star.",
