        "text": "The effective I/O fraction R I/O is the row-group survival fraction phi multiplied by the projected column byte ratio. In our numerical example with 500 columns totaling 1,000 megabytes, projecting 25 columns with 40 percent row-group survival transfers only 20 megabytes, cutting I/O by 98 percent!",
