        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "When workers process single items, eight GPUs running at twenty milliseconds per forward pass can only sustain four hundred events per second, choking sixteen thousand event Kafka partitions. But grouping sixty-four items per batch at thirty-two milliseconds elevates GPU capacity to sixteen thousand events per second—a forty-fold scaling!",
